---
import TechniquePost from "../../layouts/TechniquePost.astro"
import AnchorBuild from "../../components/UnderTheHood/AnchorBuild.astro"
import Code from "../../components/Code.astro"
---

<TechniquePost slug="anchor-hover-cards">
  <section>
    <h2 id="the-problem">The problem</h2>
    <p>
      A hover card, like GitHub's repository preview, needs a lot of JavaScript:
      timers for hover intent, listeners for focus and blur, a positioning
      library that measures the trigger, and code that flips the card when it
      would leave the viewport.
    </p>
    <p>
      HTML and CSS now cover all of it. The trigger declares what it opens, the
      browser handles hover and focus, and CSS places the card.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="the-trick">The trick</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <code>interestfor</code> on a <code>&lt;button&gt;</code>, <code
          >&lt;a href&gt;</code
        > or <code>&lt;area&gt;</code> opens the popover on hover and keyboard focus
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>popover="hint"</code> opens without closing menus and dialogs that are
        already open
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>commandfor</code> with <code>command="toggle-popover"</code> lets a
        tap open it on touch screens
      </li>
      <li>
        The invoker becomes the popover's implicit anchor, so <code
          >position-area</code
        > places the card next to the trigger without an <code>anchor-name</code
        >
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>position-try-fallbacks</code> flips it when there isn't room, <code
          >position-visibility</code
        > hides it when the trigger scrolls away
      </li>
    </ul>
    <Code
      lang="css"
      code={`.anchor > [popover] {
  inset: unset;
  margin: 0;
  position: fixed;
  position-area: var(--position-area, start end);
  position-try-fallbacks:
    flip-block,
    flip-inline,
    flip-block flip-inline;
  position-visibility: anchors-visible;
}`}
    />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="try-it">Try it</h2>
    <AnchorBuild />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="fallback">Fallback</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Without interest invokers, hover and focus do nothing. A trigger with <code
          >commandfor</code
        > still toggles the card on click, a link just follows its <code
          >href</code
        >
      </li>
      <li>
        Without <code>popover="hint"</code>, the unknown value falls back to a
        manual popover, which doesn't light dismiss
      </li>
      <li>
        Without anchor positioning, the card opens, but not next to the trigger
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</TechniquePost>
